SUMMARY:Plyometrics + Hill Sprint Technique
DESCRIPTION:Overview:\nMacros: 3600 kcal\, 170 g protein\, 550 g carbs\, 1
 00 g fat\nMacro timing: 80-110 g carbs in the 2-3 hours before running\, 
 25-35 g protein after\, and another carb-heavy meal within 2 hours.\nCate
 gory: sprint\nRun volume: 3 km\nAdjustments:\n- Adjusted for schedule con
 straints.\n\nWarm-Up:\n- 10-12 min easy plus leg swings\, A-skips\, ankli
 ng\, and 3 relaxed strides.\n\nMain Work:\n- Progression: add sprint reps
  only when contacts stay snappy and knees stay quiet the next day\; sprin
 t RPE 7-8\, never max.\n- Plyometrics: pogos 3 x 20 sec\, snap-downs 3 x 
 5\, low broad jumps 3 x 3 at crisp RPE 6-7.\n- Hill sprints: 6 x 10-12 se
 c uphill at sprint RPE 7-8\; full walk-back recovery.\n- Stop the sprint 
 set if mechanics get sloppy or knees feel sharp.\n\nOptional:\n- weighted
  sit-ups 2 x 8-12 and side plank 2 x 30 sec per side.\n\nRun:\n- Planned 
 running volume: 3 km.\n\nFueling:\n- Hit daily macros\, keep protein near
  target\, and place carbohydrates before and after training.\n\nRecovery:
 \n- Sleep window stays 22:00-06:00\; add mobility if joints feel stiff.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
