SUMMARY:Legs + Delts Accessory
DESCRIPTION:Overview:\nMacros: 3350 kcal\, 175 g protein\, 455 g carbs\, 9
 5 g fat\nMacro timing: 35-45 g protein in 4 meals\, 40-70 g carbs before 
 lifting\, and a protein-plus-carb meal after training.\nCategory: gym\nRu
 n volume: 0 km\nAdjustments:\n- Adjusted for schedule constraints.\n- Adj
 usted for recovery constraint.\n\nWarm-Up:\n- 5-6 min easy bike\, ankle r
 ocks\, band pull-aparts\, and one ramp set for each pairing.\n\nMain Work
 :\n- Progression: keep this short and low-fatigue\; stop 1-2 reps before 
 failure and leave fresher than you arrived. Recovery constraint: avoid im
 pact\, fast push-off\, and exercises that worsen next-morning symptoms.\n
 - Leg extension: 3 x 12-18 at RPE 8 paired with seated or lying hamstring
  curl 3 x 10-15 at RPE 8.\n- Lower-leg rehab: foot-intrinsic activation\,
  short-foot / arch lifts\, gentle inversion isometrics\, sole-to-sole iso
 metrics\, and double-leg heel raise isometric holds.\n- Rear delt fly or 
 reverse pec-deck: 2-3 x 15-20 at RPE 8\; if time is tight\, complete the 
 first 3 exercises and leave.\n- Chest/back/core top-up: push-ups 2 x clea
 n reps\, dips 2 x 6-10\, cable row 2 x 10-12\, face pulls 2 x 12-15\, Pal
 lof press 3 x 10 per side\, plank variations 2 x 30-45 sec\, kettlebell s
 ide bend 2 x 10-12\, around the head kettlebell 2 x 8 each way\, and weig
 hted sit-ups 2 x 8-12.\n\nFueling:\n- Hit daily macros\, keep protein nea
 r target\, and place carbohydrates before and after training.\n\nRecovery
 :\n- Sleep window stays 22:00-06:00\; add mobility if joints feel stiff.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
