SUMMARY:Core + Chest/Back Strength Capacity
DESCRIPTION:Overview:\nMacros: 3350 kcal\, 175 g protein\, 455 g carbs\, 9
 5 g fat\nMacro timing: 35-45 g protein in 4 meals\, 40-70 g carbs before 
 lifting\, and a protein-plus-carb meal after training.\nCategory: gym\nRu
 n volume: 0 km\nAdjustments:\n- Adjusted for recovery constraint.\n\nWarm
 -Up:\n- 5 min easy bike\, shoulder prep\, thoracic mobility\, hip openers
 \, and two light press/row ramp sets.\n\nMain Work:\n- Progression: this 
 is the eighth strength day in the 14-day wave\; cap work at RPE 7-8\, use
  supersets\, and trim accessories before anchor work if recovery dips. Re
 covery constraint: avoid impact\, fast push-off\, and exercises that wors
 en next-morning symptoms.\n- Chest volume: bench press 3 x 6-8\, incline 
 dumbbell press 3 x 8-10\, dumbbell press 2 x 8-10\, pec-deck 2 x 12-15\, 
 dips 2 x 6-10\, and push-ups 2 x clean reps.\n- Back volume: lat pulldown
  or pull-ups 3 x 8-12\, cable row or chest-supported row 3 x 8-12\, face 
 pulls 2 x 12-15\, and rear delt fly or reverse pec-deck 2 x 15-20.\n- Leg
  maintenance: hip thrust or glute bridge 3 x 8-12\, leg extension 2 x 12-
 15\, and seated or lying hamstring curl 2 x 10-15 at RPE 7.\n- Core volum
 e: Pallof press 3 x 10 per side\, side plank 2 x 30 sec per side\, plank 
 variations 2 x 30-45 sec\, hanging leg raises 2-3 sets\, weighted sit-ups
  2 x 8-12\, and kettlebell side bend or around the head kettlebell 2 x 10
 .\n\nFueling:\n- Hit daily macros\, keep protein near target\, and place 
 carbohydrates before and after training.\n\nRecovery:\n- Sleep window sta
 ys 22:00-06:00\; add mobility if joints feel stiff.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
